[Glimt Decoder]
Name=Photoshop (ImageMagick)
Comment=The picture of a Photoshop file as saved (its composite), through ImageMagick
Extensions=psd;psb
# %f[0]: the composite, the picture as last saved, not its layers one by one; ImageMagick's PSD
# reader also reads large documents (.psb). PAM keeps transparency.
# The format is named before the path ("psd:"): without it ImageMagick goes by what the bytes
# say, and a file from the internet named .psd could reach Ghostscript or another coder.
# ImageMagick 7 names the program magick instead of convert.
Exec=convert psd:%f[0] -depth 8 pam:-
